From 945ea5ad0dba300699e8b550f4b7b735b9a569c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:47:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): attach this host's core-update hold only to
 cards it leases [daveey]

Ready-card chat notices (chat_wait_unclaimed) blamed the hub's own core-update
swap for pool cards the hub never leases: 41 such notices on pool-placed cards
in the Board replica, 11-11 21:47Z to 11-15 16:40Z (task t_fc957aa5f46a6e47).

Example: 2026-11-15 16:40:48Z, t_826b414bdb02d4ef (runs_on capability:core-ship,
pool:worker) was told "claims are held for a pending Hermes update" during the
hub's 185 s swap. Pool workers claimed cards the whole time (claimed events
16:36-16:43Z from worker-1..6 and -8). The card was really waiting on the
openai-codex pacing hold and queue order. Notices post once per ready episode,
so the true reason was never sent.

Five whys:
1. Why the wrong sentence? The payload carried core_update_hold, which
   notice_text prints before the queue/pacing sentence, and post_notice
   recorded admission core_update_hold.
2. Why did the payload carry it? kanban_chat_wait.sweep() reads this host's
   update_hold() once and merges it into every due card's extra.
3. Why every card? c7eb57bb4e2 ("Explain active update drains in ready-card
   notices") assumed the host's hold stops every ready card's claims.
4. Why is that false? The hold (agent.core_update_drain.active_hold) only
   stops this host's dispatcher. Pool and remote-placed cards are leased by
   other machines, which keep claiming.
5. Why was nothing checking? post_notice computes the card's queue place
   (lane) but never compared it with the host the hold belongs to.

Fix: post_notice drops core_update_* from extra unless the card's place is
lane "local" (this host leases it). Pool (worker_pool), remote-placed
(machine) and unplaceable cards get exactly the notice they get with no hold
active: queue place, busy-pool or pacing admission. Hub-leasable cards keep
the hold sentence and core_update_hold admission. An unknown place (position
lookup failed) also drops the hold, since it does not prove this host leases
the card. No change to the drain itself or to worker-side holds.

Tests:
- test_kanban_drain_wait_notice: a pool card that falls due in a real sweep
  under an active hub hold gets the same payload and text as with no hold
  (busy and non-busy pool); a worker_pool card gets "waiting for a pool
  worker"; a local card under the hold keeps the hold sentence and admission;
  with no hold a local card keeps the capacity notice.
- test_kanban_label_backlog_wait / test_kanban_notice_pacing_admission: two
  existing tests asserted the defect (hold over a pool card's busy-pool
  reason); they now assert the pool reason, and the hold precedence on a
  local card. New test for the incident shape: paced pool card under the
  hold gets the llm_pacing notice.
- RED on origin/main: 4 of the new/changed pool assertions fail; GREEN: the
  21 test files importing kanban_parent_unclaimed / kanban_chat_wait /
  core_update_hold pass (414 tests). scripts/check --base origin/main ok.
